{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba skills/adversarial/SKILL.md | sed -n '1,220p'\"","aggregated_output":"error: Can't create the symlink for multishells at \"/run/user/1001/fnm_multishells/8_1782867814826\". Maybe there are some issues with permissions for the directory? Read-only file system (os error 30)\n     1\t---\n     2\tname: adversarial\n     3\tuser-invokable: true\n     4\tdescription: Run a dual-agent adversarial code review. Dispatches a Codex reviewer in parallel with a Claude reviewer. Both review the same diff independently. Surfaces disagreements after both complete.\n     5\t---\n     6\t\n     7\t# Adversarial Review\n     8\t\n     9\tRun two independent reviewers against the same diff, then compare their reports. This skill is standalone and does not depend on the mission system.\n    10\t\n    11\t## Startup Config\n    12\t\n    13\tAt startup, resolve the Darkfactory repo root from the skill symlink and read `default_model` from its `config.yaml`. If the file or key is absent, use `gpt-5.5`.\n    14\t\n    15\t```bash\n    16\tDARKFACTORY_ROOT=\"$(cd \"$(readlink \"$HOME/.claude/skills/adversarial\")/../..\" 2>/dev/null && pwd -P)\"\n    17\tDEFAULT_MODEL=$(awk -F: '/^[[:space:]]*default_model[[:space:]]*:/ { gsub(/^[[:space:]]+|[[:space:]]+$/, \"\", $2); print $2; exit }' \"$DARKFACTORY_ROOT/config.yaml\" 2>/dev/null)\n    18\t: \"${DEFAULT_MODEL:=gpt-5.5}\"\n    19\t```\n    20\t\n    21\t## Input Modes\n    22\t\n    23\tDetermine the mode from the optional argument:\n    24\t\n    25\t- No argument: review `git diff HEAD` for all staged and unstaged working tree changes.\n    26\t- PR number, such as `/adversarial 42`: review `gh pr diff 42`.\n    27\t- File path, such as `/adversarial path/to/file.ts`: review `git diff HEAD -- path/to/file.ts`.\n    28\t\n    29\tTreat an all-digit argument as a PR number. Treat any other non-empty argument as a file path.\n    30\t\n    31\t## Report Paths\n    32\t\n    33\tBefore dispatching reviewers, choose report paths:\n    34\t\n    35\t- If the repo contains a Darkfactory mission directory matching `openspec/changes/*/mission/`, excluding any path that contains `openspec/changes/archive/`, write reports under that mission:\n    36\t  - `mission/validations/adversarial-codex.md`\n    37\t  - `mission/validations/adversarial-claude.md`\n    38\t  - `mission/logs/adversarial-codex.log`\n    39\t- Otherwise, write reports to temp files and tell the user both paths:\n    40\t  - `/tmp/adversarial-codex-<timestamp>.md`\n    41\t  - `/tmp/adversarial-claude-<timestamp>.md`\n    42\t  - `/tmp/adversarial-codex-<timestamp>.log`\n    43\t\n    44\tWhen a mission path is used, create `mission/validations/` and `mission/logs/` if needed.\n    45\t\n    46\t## Step 1: Get The Diff\n    47\t\n    48\tRun exactly one diff command based on the input mode:\n    49\t\n    50\t```bash\n    51\tgit diff HEAD\n    52\tgh pr diff <number>\n    53\tgit diff HEAD -- <path>\n    54\t```\n    55\t\n    56\tIf the diff is empty, report `No changes to review` and stop.\n    57\t\n    58\tSave the diff content once and pass the identical content to both reviewers.\n    59\t\n    60\t## Step 2: Dispatch Codex Reviewer\n    61\t\n    62\tStart Codex first and do not block before launching Claude. Dispatch with `darkfactory-dispatch --json` in a single Bash tool call with `run_in_background: true`. The backgrounded script must capture the dispatcher output, parse `.status`, remove the prompt file, and print a final stdout line beginning with `REVIEW_COMPLETE` or `REVIEW_FAILED`.\n    63\t\n    64\t`--output \"<codex-report-path>\"` writes Codex's **final message** to that path. So the prompt asks Codex to return the report as its final message and not write any files itself -- if Codex wrote the report to that path with its own tools, its closing assistant message would overwrite it. (Claude in Step 3 has no `--output`, so it writes its file directly.)\n    65\t\n    66\tPrompt:\n    67\t\n    68\t```text\n    69\tYou are an adversarial code reviewer. Review the following diff for bugs, logic errors, security issues, and missing edge cases. Group findings by severity: critical, warning, nit. Cite file:line for each finding. Return the full report as your final message -- do not write any files.\n    70\t\n    71\t<diff content>\n    72\t```\n    73\t\n    74\tDispatch command:\n    75\t\n    76\t```bash\n    77\tREPORT_PATH=\"<codex-report-path>\"\n    78\tLOG_PATH=\"<codex-log-path>\"\n    79\tPROMPT_PATH=$(mktemp /tmp/adversarial-prompt.XXXXXX)\n    80\t# Use >| : mktemp pre-creates the file, and zsh `noclobber` makes a bare `>` fail on it.\n    81\tcat >| \"$PROMPT_PATH\" << 'PROMPT'\n    82\tYou are an adversarial code reviewer. Review the following diff for bugs, logic errors, security issues, and missing edge cases. Group findings by severity: critical, warning, nit. Cite file:line for each finding. Return the full report as your final message -- do not write any files.\n    83\t\n    84\t<diff content>\n    85\tPROMPT\n    86\t\n    87\tDISPATCH_RESULT=$(darkfactory-dispatch \\\n    88\t  --model \"$DEFAULT_MODEL\" \\\n    89\t  --effort high \\\n    90\t  --timeout 900 \\\n    91\t  --sandbox workspace-write \\\n    92\t  --prompt-file \"$PROMPT_PATH\" \\\n    93\t  --output \"$REPORT_PATH\" \\\n    94\t  --cwd \"$(pwd)\" \\\n    95\t  --log \"$LOG_PATH\" \\\n    96\t  --json 2>>\"$LOG_PATH\")\n    97\t\n    98\trm -f \"$PROMPT_PATH\"\n    99\t\n   100\tif [ -z \"$DISPATCH_RESULT\" ]; then\n   101\t  echo \"REVIEW_FAILED: dispatcher crashed with no output. Log: $LOG_PATH\"\n   102\telse\n   103\t  DISPATCH_STATUS=$(printf '%s\\n' \"$DISPATCH_RESULT\" | jq -r '.status')\n   104\t  DISPATCH_ERROR=$(printf '%s\\n' \"$DISPATCH_RESULT\" | jq -r '.error.message // empty')\n   105\t\n   106\t  if [ \"$DISPATCH_STATUS\" = \"completed\" ] && [ -f \"$REPORT_PATH\" ]; then\n   107\t    echo \"REVIEW_COMPLETE: report written\"\n   108\t  else\n   109\t    echo \"REVIEW_FAILED: dispatch status $DISPATCH_STATUS${DISPATCH_ERROR:+; error: $DISPATCH_ERROR}; report $([ -f \"$REPORT_PATH\" ] && echo present || echo missing). Log: $LOG_PATH\"\n   110\t  fi\n   111\tfi\n   112\t```\n   113\t\n   114\t## Step 3: Dispatch Claude Reviewer\n   115\t\n   116\tWhile Codex is running in the background, dispatch Claude via the Agent tool. Give Claude the same diff content and the same reviewer prompt, changing only the report path to `<claude-report-path>`.\n   117\t\n   118\tClaude must write its report to `adversarial-claude.md` at the selected report path.\n   119\t\n   120\t## Step 4: Collect Results\n   121\t\n   122\tAfter Claude finishes, retrieve the backgrounded Codex Bash call's stdout with BashOutput. If the Codex shell task has not completed yet, collect it again after the task completion notification.\n   123\t\n   124\tTreat a final stdout line beginning with `REVIEW_COMPLETE` as success. Only then read the Codex report file. Treat a final stdout line beginning with `REVIEW_FAILED`, or a dispatcher `.status` of `failed` or `timed_out`, as a Codex review failure. On failure, report the dispatch failure and log path instead of claiming the Codex report completed.\n   125\t\n   126\tFor each report, count findings by severity:\n   127\t\n   128\t- `critical`\n   129\t- `warning`\n   130\t- `nit`\n   131\t\n   132\tFind disagreements:\n   133\t\n   134\t- Findings that appear in the Codex report but not the Claude report.\n   135\t- Findings that appear in the Claude report but not the Codex report.\n   136\t- Findings both report but classify with different severity.\n   137\t\n   138\tCompare findings by affected file, line, and issue description. Minor wording differences do not count as a disagreement when the same bug is clearly being described.\n   139\t\n   140\t## User Output\n   141\t\n   142\tPresent the final result in this format:\n   143\t\n   144\t```text\n   145\tAdversarial review complete.\n   146\t\n   147\tCodex reviewer: N critical, M warnings, P nits\n   148\t  Full report: <path>\n   149\t\n   150\tClaude reviewer: N critical, M warnings, P nits\n   151\t  Full report: <path>\n   152\t\n   153\tDisagreements (flagged by one reviewer only):\n   154\t- [Codex only] <finding>\n   155\t- [Claude only] <finding>\n   156\t\n   157\tReview the full reports and decide what to address.\n   158\t```\n   159\t\n   160\tIf there are no disagreements, write:\n   161\t\n   162\t```text\n   163\tDisagreements (flagged by one reviewer only):\n   164\t- None\n   165\t```\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
