{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_27","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n \\\"parent|PDEATH|process group|process-group|setpgid|SIGKILL|SIGTERM|timeout|heartbeat|output|Exit codes|log|status.json|control\\\" tools/darkfactory-dispatch/README.md tools/darkfactory-dispatch/CLAUDE.md openspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only -g '*.md'\"","aggregated_output":"error: Can't create the symlink for multishells at \"/run/user/1001/fnm_multishells/8_1782867947308\". Maybe there are some issues with permissions for the directory? Read-only file system (os error 30)\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/README.md:3:A process supervisor for Codex CLI subprocesses. Sits between the orchestrator and a Codex worker, handling process group isolation, two-phase timeout, heartbeat events, and structured result reporting.\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/README.md:9:Without the dispatcher, the orchestrator calls `codex exec` directly as a raw subprocess. If Codex hangs (stdin stall, long reasoning silence, subprocess wedge), the orchestrator waits forever. There are no heartbeats, no timeout, no structured results -- just a log file and hope.\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/README.md:13:- **Isolates the process group** so killing Codex also kills any shell commands it spawned\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/README.md:14:- **Enforces a two-phase timeout** -- SIGTERM at the soft timeout, SIGKILL after the grace period\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/README.md:15:- **Emits heartbeat events** every 15 seconds so the orchestrator can distinguish \"thinking\" from \"dead\"\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/README.md:31:  │ spawns codex exec --json ... in its own process group\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/README.md:33:  │ emits heartbeats to stderr every 15s\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/README.md:34:  │ enforces two-phase timeout (SIGTERM → grace → SIGKILL)\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/README.md:40:  │ writes handoff report to --output path\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/README.md:82:  --timeout 1800 \\\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/README.md:86:  --output handoff.md \\\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/README.md:88:  --log dispatch.log \\\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/README.md:89:  --json 2>>dispatch.log\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/README.md:92:The dispatch result is a single JSON object on stdout. In `--json` mode stdout carries **only** that one object; all events, heartbeats, and diagnostics go to stderr. Do not merge the two streams (`2>&1`) when parsing the result -- the concatenated event lines will make `jq` or `serde_json` fail. Redirect stderr elsewhere (e.g. `2>>dispatch.log`), as the examples above do.\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/README.md:101:  \"output\": \"handoff.md\",\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/README.md:102:  \"output_exists\": true,\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/README.md:106:    \"output\": 1407,\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/README.md:125:{\"type\":\"heartbeat\",\"dispatch_id\":\"...\",\"ts\":\"...\",\"elapsed_s\":15,\"last_activity\":\"running: cargo test\"}\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/README.md:128:{\"type\":\"heartbeat\",\"dispatch_id\":\"...\",\"ts\":\"...\",\"elapsed_s\":30,\"last_activity\":\"writing: src/lib.rs\"}\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/README.md:129:{\"type\":\"timeout_warning\",\"dispatch_id\":\"...\",\"ts\":\"...\",\"elapsed_s\":1800}\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/README.md:133:To watch progress live, redirect stderr to the log file and tail it:\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/README.md:136:darkfactory-dispatch ... --json 2>>dispatch.log &\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/README.md:137:tail -f dispatch.log\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/README.md:146:| `--timeout` | `900` | Seconds before soft timeout fires (SIGTERM) |\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/README.md:147:| `--grace` | half of timeout, min 1s | Seconds between soft timeout and hard timeout (SIGKILL) |\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/README.md:148:| `--heartbeat` | `15` | Seconds between heartbeat events emitted to stderr |\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/README.md:153:| `--output` | (none) | Path for Codex to write results (passed to `-o`) |\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/README.md:155:| `--log` | (none) | File to capture Codex stdout and stderr |\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/README.md:158:## Two-phase timeout\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/README.md:160:The dispatcher enforces a configurable two-phase timeout:\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/README.md:162:1. **Soft timeout** (at `--timeout` seconds): Sends SIGTERM to the process group and emits a `timeout_warning` event. The worker has a chance to flush partial results.\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/README.md:163:2. **Hard timeout** (at `--timeout` + `--grace` seconds): Sends SIGKILL to the process group. The worker is forcibly terminated.\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/README.md:165:The grace period defaults to half the timeout with a minimum of 1 second.\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/README.md:167:If the worker exits cleanly after SIGTERM (during the grace period), the dispatch result reports `timed_out` with the worker's final output preserved.\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/README.md:171:Every Codex worker runs in its own process group (via `setpgid`). When the dispatcher sends SIGTERM or SIGKILL, the signal goes to the entire group -- not just the Codex process, but every shell command and subprocess it spawned. This prevents orphaned processes from accumulating.\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/README.md:175:The dispatcher detects when its parent process (the orchestrator) dies and kills the worker to prevent orphans:\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/README.md:177:- **macOS**: Uses kqueue with `EVFILT_PROC` + `NOTE_EXIT` to watch the parent PID\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/README.md:178:- **Linux**: Uses `PR_SET_PDEATHSIG` to arrange SIGKILL on parent death\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/README.md:180:## Exit codes\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/README.md:192:| `completed` | Worker exited 0 and output file exists (if `--output` was specified) |\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/README.md:193:| `timed_out` | Two-phase timeout fired. `error.retryable` is true. |\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/README.md:194:| `failed` | Worker exited non-zero, output file missing, or spawn error |\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/CLAUDE.md:3:Rust process supervisor for Codex CLI subprocesses. Spawns `codex exec` with process group isolation, two-phase timeout, NDJSON heartbeat events, and structured JSON results.\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/CLAUDE.md:12:                  timeout select loop, heartbeat, result finalization\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/CLAUDE.md:13:  supervisor.rs   Process spawning, process groups, signals, GracefulStop,\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/CLAUDE.md:14:                  parent-death detection (kqueue on macOS, prctl on Linux)\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/CLAUDE.md:17:  event.rs        NDJSON event emitter, heartbeat ticker\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/CLAUDE.md:21:  engine.rs       Timeout and heartbeat tests with mock child processes\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/CLAUDE.md:38:- **Gallant pattern** (boundary rule): Engine owns ALL dispatch logic. CLI MUST only parse input, call engine, and format output. This governs which module a function belongs in.\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/CLAUDE.md:44:- **Output**: Stdout for machine-readable data (DispatchResult JSON), stderr for diagnostics (heartbeats, events, warnings).\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/CLAUDE.md:45:- **No double-logging**: Propagate errors with `?`. Log only when the error is finally handled. NEVER log and propagate.\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/CLAUDE.md:46:- **Exit codes**: 0 = success (completed), 1 = dispatch failure (failed, timed_out), 2 = CLI error (bad args, missing binary).\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/CLAUDE.md:57:| supervisor | `internal/supervisor/reaper_linux.go` | PR_SET_PDEATHSIG via prctl |\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/CLAUDE.md:58:| engine | `internal/engine/loop.go:167-981` | Dispatch function, two-phase timeout, heartbeat |\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/CLAUDE.md:60:| engine | `internal/event/event.go` | Event emitter, heartbeat ticker |\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/CLAUDE.md:66:Tests required when a change could break silently (process management, NDJSON parsing, timeout logic, CLI argument construction, result serialization). NOT required for docs-only changes.\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/contract.md:7:- [ ] [output] `grep -rnE \"fn graceful_stop|fn heartbeat_ticker|struct CancellationToken|fn emit_heartbeat\\b|StreamMode::(Silent|Verbose)|StdinMode::Piped|fn pid\\b\" src/` returns no matches (the named dead APIs are gone).\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/contract.md:11:## Task 2: Remove the async subsystem and engine status/control\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/contract.md:15:- [ ] [execution] After a normal `--json` dispatch with no user `--log`/`--output` under those paths, no files exist under `/tmp/darkfactory-dispatch/` or `~/.darkfactory/dispatches/` created by that run. <!-- dispatch-cli/5 -->\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/contract.md:17:- [ ] [output] `grep -rnE \"control\\.json|write_status_json_atomic|status_dir|store_dir|LiveStatus|enum Commands|async_mode\" tools/darkfactory-dispatch/src/` returns no matches — the async/status/control internals are gone from the source. This directly verifies the status.json/store/control removal (the behavioral \"no files after a dispatch\" check alone can pass against the OLD code, which writes `/tmp/darkfactory-dispatch/<id>/status.json` mid-run and deletes it on exit) and the control-file channel removal (its path is keyed by a per-run dispatch id and cannot be pre-planted). <!-- dispatch-cli/6 -->\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/contract.md:19:- [ ] [execution] A worker that exits 0 without creating the requested `--output` file yields a JSON result with `status` `\"failed\"`. <!-- synchronous-dispatch/2 -->\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/contract.md:21:- [ ] [execution] A dispatch with `--output P` writes the worker artifact to `P` and the JSON result reports `output` `P` with `output_exists` true; `--cwd`, `--log`, `--grace`, and `--heartbeat` are accepted without a parse error. <!-- dispatch-cli/4, dispatch-cli/3 -->\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/contract.md:22:- [ ] [output] `Cargo.toml` declares no `tracing` or `tracing-subscriber` dependency, and neither appears as a direct dependency in `Cargo.lock`.\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/contract.md:27:- [ ] [output] `grep -E \"\\-\\-async|darkfactory-dispatch (status|wait|result)|async_started\" skills/adversarial/SKILL.md` returns no matches. <!-- adversarial-sync-review/1 -->\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/contract.md:28:- [ ] [output] `skills/adversarial/SKILL.md` dispatches its reviewer with `--json` run via `run_in_background` and collected with `BashOutput`. <!-- adversarial-sync-review/1 -->\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/contract.md:29:- [ ] [output] `skills/adversarial/SKILL.md` reads the dispatch result `.status` from the captured output and emits a `REVIEW_COMPLETE` marker on `completed` and a `REVIEW_FAILED` marker on `failed`/`timed_out`. <!-- adversarial-sync-review/2, adversarial-sync-review/3 -->\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/contract.md:34:- [ ] [output] `tools/darkfactory-dispatch/README.md` contains no async-mode section, no `status`/`wait`/`result` lifecycle documentation, and no dispatch-store section, and it still contains the progress-monitoring (`tail -f`) guidance.\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/contract.md:35:- [ ] [output] `tools/darkfactory-dispatch/CLAUDE.md` repo map no longer references the `status`/`wait`/`result` subcommands, async routing, the watchdog, or `LiveStatus`.\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/contract.md:40:- [ ] [output] `tests/supervisor.rs` still contains the two-phase-timeout and process-group-teardown test functions (and the parent-death handling test), and `tests/engine.rs` still contains the heartbeat-emission test function — the retained supervision tests were not deleted. <!-- synchronous-dispatch/5, synchronous-dispatch/6, synchronous-dispatch/7, synchronous-dispatch/8 -->\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/contract.md:41:- [ ] [execution] `cargo test` runs and passes the full `tests/supervisor.rs` and `tests/engine.rs` suites, which exercise the two-phase timeout, process-group teardown, heartbeat emission, and parent-death watch. <!-- synchronous-dispatch/5, synchronous-dispatch/6, synchronous-dispatch/7, synchronous-dispatch/8 -->\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/contract.md:42:- [ ] [execution] A dispatch run as `darkfactory-dispatch ... --log f 2>>f` produces a file `f` containing both the worker's output and the dispatcher's heartbeat events. <!-- synchronous-dispatch/9 -->\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/design.md:12:                                               ├─ supervisor.rs  (setpgid, signals, parent-death)\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/design.md:13:                                               └─ event.rs       (heartbeats + NDJSON → stderr)\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/design.md:18:The load-bearing supervision — process-group isolation, two-phase SIGTERM/SIGKILL timeout while draining output, 15s heartbeat emission, parent-death detection, NDJSON parse to a structured result — is sound and stays untouched.\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/design.md:20:**How the change fits:** the engine currently carries a second, optional path (an async lifecycle backed by a `store_dir` on the spec) plus a watchdog select-arm that reads a `control.json` and writes `status.json`. The change removes that second path and the watchdog arm, collapsing the engine to the single synchronous path that production already uses. Removing `store_dir` makes parent-death always-on (it was disabled only in async mode). No new modules or types are introduced.\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/design.md:28:| `main.rs` | narrow — process entry (`run()`) | sequencing of cli → engine, exit-code mapping | process lifecycle separate from dispatch logic |\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/design.md:30:| `engine.rs` | narrow — `dispatch(spec) -> DispatchResult` | the async select loop, two-phase timeout sequencing, NDJSON draining | dispatch orchestration separate from OS-level control |\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/design.md:31:| `supervisor.rs` | narrow — `SupervisorBuilder`/`RunHandle` | `setpgid`, group signaling, parent-death (`PR_SET_PDEATHSIG`/kqueue) | OS/process-group details isolated in one place |\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/design.md:32:| `event.rs` | narrow — `Emitter` | event serialization and stderr writing | event/IO separate from dispatch logic |\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/design.md:35:What narrows in this change (no module added or removed): `cli.rs` loses `--async`, the `Commands` enum/subcommands, and the store helpers; `engine.rs` loses the watchdog arm (the control-file read and the in-loop status write) AND the separate post-dispatch status write — both `write_status_json_atomic` call sites — plus the `store_dir` branching, so `write_status_json_atomic`/`status_dir` are removed entirely and no status file is written at any point; `supervisor.rs` loses `graceful_stop`/`RunHandle::pid` (and the now-dead `RunState.pid` field)/`StdinMode::Piped`/singular `arg`; `event.rs` loses `CancellationToken`/`heartbeat_ticker`/`StreamMode::Silent|Verbose`/`emit_heartbeat` and its local heartbeat constant; and `types.rs` loses the `LiveStatus` status-store type (with its `cli.rs`/`engine.rs` imports and uses).\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/design.md:37:## Type Catalog\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/design.md:41:| `DispatchSpec` | Inputs to one dispatch (command, timeout, grace, heartbeat, sandbox, log, output, cwd). The `store_dir` field is removed. | `types.rs` |\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/design.md:42:| `DispatchResult` | The structured result emitted on stdout (status, exit code, signal, duration, tokens, activity, output). | `types.rs` |\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/design.md:47:| `HarnessEvent` / `EventKind` | Events emitted to stderr (heartbeat, tool activity, dispatch end). | `event.rs` |\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/design.md:72:`/adversarial` conversion note: because the dispatcher exits non-zero on `failed`/`timed_out`, the converted skill must capture the dispatcher's stdout (the JSON result) separately from the process exit, then parse `.status` from that captured stdout to decide `REVIEW_COMPLETE` vs `REVIEW_FAILED` — it must not treat a non-zero background-shell exit as an unparseable error. This mirrors the mission Phase 9 reviewer script: `DISPATCH_RESULT=$(... --json 2>>log)` then parse `.status`.\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/design.md:80:- **Tests to delete** (their subjects are removed): async/lifecycle tests in `tests/cli.rs` (help-expects-`--async`, mutual-exclusion, `status`/`wait`/`result` unknown-id, async-flow, orphan, pruning); `control_file_abort_*` in `tests/engine.rs`; `stream_mode_filtering` and `heartbeat_ticker_can_be_cancelled` in `src/event.rs`; `graceful_stop_*` and singular `.arg` uses in `tests/supervisor.rs`.\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/design.md:81:- **Tests to keep/adapt:** supervisor process-group + two-phase-timeout tests; engine NDJSON/result tests; `tests/smoketest.sh` (sync `--json` only — should survive unchanged).\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/design.md:82:- **New tests (minimal):** small integration tests for the new observable behaviors — `--async`/lifecycle subcommands rejected, no files under the `/tmp` store, a planted `control.json` is ignored. No-files assertions run against an isolated `HOME`/baseline.\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/design.md:86:The current structure is sound; the meaningful coupling being removed is the `store_dir` threading (`cli → DispatchSpec → engine`) and the watchdog select-arm. **Compile-safety constraint:** `engine.rs` reads `spec.store_dir` for status-dir selection, cleanup, parent-death, and both status writes, so `DispatchSpec.store_dir` cannot be removed before its engine readers — the field and its consumers must land together in one compile-safe step. The safe removal order (drives task ordering in Phase 4.4): (1) dead test-only code first — risk-free, independent; (2) **one compile-safe step** removing the async subsystem (`--async`, the `Commands` subcommands, store helpers, clap `conflicts_with`, the `tracing` deps) together with the engine's `store_dir` field/branches, the watchdog arm (control read + in-loop status write), the post-dispatch status write, `write_status_json_atomic`/`status_dir`, and the `LiveStatus` type — all coupled through `store_dir`/status — while moving `cli::failed_start_result` (dispatch `Err` → `failed` JSON) into the unified sync path so spawn errors still emit one JSON result; (3) the `/adversarial` consumer; (4) README/CLAUDE.md docs. Every task must compile (`cargo build` green) at its own commit.\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/tasks.md:8:  Produces: removed dead APIs (`graceful_stop`, `RunHandle::pid` + the `RunState.pid` field, `StdinMode::Piped`, singular `SupervisorBuilder::arg`, `CancellationToken`, `heartbeat_ticker`, `StreamMode::Silent|Verbose`, `Emitter::emit_heartbeat`, the event-local heartbeat constant) and the tests that only exercise them; `#[expect(dead_code)]` annotations resolved as `cargo build` flags them\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/tasks.md:12:- [x] Task 2: Remove the async subsystem and engine status/control in one compile-safe step\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/tasks.md:15:  Produces: synchronous-only CLI (no `--async`; no `status`/`wait`/`result` subcommands; no store helpers; clap `conflicts_with` removed); engine with no watchdog arm, no `control.json` read, and no `status.json` writes (BOTH `write_status_json_atomic` sites), no `store_dir`/`status_dir`; `DispatchSpec` without `store_dir`; `LiveStatus` removed; `tracing` + `tracing-subscriber` deps dropped from `Cargo.toml` AND `Cargo.lock` regenerated so the removed direct deps are gone; `cli::failed_start_result` moved into the unified sync path (dispatch `Err` -> `failed` JSON on stdout, non-zero exit); parent-death always-on; integration tests added for the new observable behaviors — `--async` and `status`/`wait`/`result` rejected (non-zero exit, no JSON, no files), no files under `/tmp/darkfactory-dispatch/` or `~/.darkfactory/dispatches/` after a normal dispatch, a planted `control.json` is ignored, a spawn error yields a `failed` JSON result, pre-existing files seeded under `/tmp/darkfactory-dispatch/` and `~/.darkfactory/dispatches/` are left unchanged by a dispatch (no pruning/deletion), and the retained flags `--output`/`--cwd`/`--log`/`--grace`/`--heartbeat` are accepted and functional\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/tasks.md:38:  Produces: `tests/smoketest.sh` verified/extended to exercise the primary synchronous `--json` dispatch flow end-to-end with no async surface; the existing supervision tests — two-phase timeout, process-group teardown, and heartbeat emission in `tests/supervisor.rs` and `tests/engine.rs` — are retained and pass, verifying the preserved supervision (the synchronous-dispatch scenarios for timeout, process group, heartbeat, and log capture); the run is documented in the handoff\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/proposal.md:5:`tools/darkfactory-dispatch` is a Rust process supervisor for Codex workers (2,990 LOC). Its supervision core is solid, but it carries roughly 1,000 lines of incidental machinery on top: an async-dispatch subsystem (`--async`, `status`/`wait`/`result` subcommands, and a `~/.darkfactory/dispatches/<ulid>/` store), a control-file abort channel, redundant `/tmp` status.json writes, and dead code that only its own tests exercise.\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/proposal.md:7:This machinery is not free. The async lifecycle has exactly one consumer, the `/adversarial` skill, and it uses it incorrectly: the dispatch id never escapes the background shell, so a review that actually passed is reported as failed. The control-file and status files sit in a world-readable `/tmp` path, so any local user can read a dispatch's progress or plant an abort file to kill it. And the async surface duplicates Claude Code's own `run_in_background` + `BashOutput` primitive, which the mission flow already uses for the same job.\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/proposal.md:13:- Remove the async-dispatch subsystem: the `--async` flag, the `status`/`wait`/`result` subcommands, and the `~/.darkfactory/dispatches/<ulid>/` store (status.json, result.json, host.pid, events.jsonl), including its 7-day pruning. Pre-existing dispatch-store and `/tmp` dispatch directories from past runs are left untouched (they are ephemeral; no migration or one-time cleanup is performed).\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/proposal.md:14:- Remove the control-file abort channel (the `control.json` watchdog and its handling).\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/proposal.md:15:- Remove the now-dead automatic `/tmp` status.json writes and the watchdog interval that drove them, so the dispatcher no longer creates status or control files under its world-readable `/tmp` dispatch directory. (This concerns the dispatcher's own automatic writes, not user-specified `--log` paths, which are unchanged.)\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/proposal.md:16:- Remove dead test-only code (`graceful_stop`, `RunHandle::pid`, `StdinMode::Piped`, singular `SupervisorBuilder::arg`, `CancellationToken`, `heartbeat_ticker`, `StreamMode::Silent`/`Verbose`, `Emitter::emit_heartbeat`, the event-local heartbeat constant) and delete the tests that only exercise it. The heartbeat-named items here are the unused/superseded helpers; the live heartbeat path (`emit_heartbeat_with_interval`, driven by the inline heartbeat interval in the engine select loop) is NOT touched — see the preservation bullet below.\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/proposal.md:19:- Preserve all load-bearing supervision unchanged: process-group isolation, two-phase SIGTERM/SIGKILL timeout with output draining, 15-second heartbeat emission (the live `emit_heartbeat_with_interval` path, independent of the removed helpers), parent-death detection (now always on), the structured JSON result on stdout, the `--log` flag, and the `--grace`/`--heartbeat` flags.\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/proposal.md:25:- **Replace the binary with a shell script.** Rejected: the load-bearing robustness (process-group teardown, two-phase timeout while draining NDJSON, parent-death detection) is exactly what shell does unreliably. That fragility is why the binary exists.\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/proposal.md:26:- **Also fix the deferred core bugs (orphan-on-error / no `kill_on_drop`, unbounded stderr await) in this pass.** Rejected for scope: they live in the kept core and deserve their own focused change; bundling them widens the diff and the risk. (Removing async partially mitigates the Linux orphan case by leaving parent-death always on.)\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/proposal.md:31:- `synchronous-dispatch` — supervised synchronous dispatch of a Codex worker: two-phase timeout, 15s heartbeat events, process-group teardown, parent-death cleanup, structured JSON result on stdout, and log streaming via `--log`.\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/proposal.md:32:- `dispatch-cli` — the command-line surface after the cut: the retained flags work; the removed `--async` flag and `status`/`wait`/`result` subcommands are rejected by the CLI parser with a non-zero exit and a usage error, producing no JSON result and no filesystem side effects; and a dispatch with no user-specified `--log` path under those locations writes no files under the old `/tmp` dispatch directory or `~/.darkfactory/dispatches/`.\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/reviews/phase3-proposal.md:10:- **HIGH (Ambiguity): Heartbeat removal vs preserved heartbeat behavior.** The removal list named `heartbeat_ticker`, `Emitter::emit_heartbeat`, and the event-local heartbeat constant while the proposal also preserves \"15s heartbeat emission\" — an implementer could delete the live path. **Fixed:** named the live path `emit_heartbeat_with_interval` (inline engine interval) in both the removal and preservation bullets, marking the listed items as unused/superseded helpers.\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/reviews/phase3-proposal.md:11:- **MEDIUM (Coverage): `/tmp` write ban unclear vs preserved `--log`.** **Fixed:** scoped the requirement to the dispatcher's *automatic* status/control writes under its `/tmp` dispatch dir, explicitly excluding user-specified `--log` paths.\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/reviews/phase3-proposal.md:17:- **LOW (Ambiguity): \"normal dispatch\" boundary vs `--log`.** **Resolved:** defined as a dispatch with no user-specified `--log` path under those locations.\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/coverage-audit.md:9:| 2 | Remove the control-file abort channel (`control.json` watchdog) | dispatch-cli: \"A planted control file cannot abort a dispatch\" | Task 2 | COVERED |\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/coverage-audit.md:10:| 3 | Remove the now-dead automatic `/tmp` status.json writes + the watchdog interval | dispatch-cli: \"No automatic filesystem side effects\" (no files under `/tmp/darkfactory-dispatch/`) | Task 2 | COVERED |\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/coverage-audit.md:12:| 4b | Live `emit_heartbeat_with_interval` path NOT touched (heartbeats preserved) | synchronous-dispatch: \"Heartbeat emission\" | Task 5 (retained engine heartbeat tests pass) | COVERED |\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/coverage-audit.md:15:| 7 | Preserve all load-bearing supervision (process group, two-phase timeout, heartbeat, parent-death always-on, structured result incl. spawn-error JSON, `--log`, `--grace`/`--heartbeat`) | synchronous-dispatch: all 6 requirements (sync result, timeout, heartbeat, process-group, parent-death, log capture) | Task 2 (preserves while cutting; spawn-error JSON; retained-flag + pre-existing-file tests), Task 5 (retained timeout/process-group/heartbeat tests pass) | COVERED |\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/reviews/phase4.5-coverage-audit.md:11:- **HIGH:** row 7 \"preserve supervision\" was asserted but not tested → Task 5 now explicitly retains and passes the existing two-phase-timeout / process-group / heartbeat tests (`tests/supervisor.rs`, `tests/engine.rs`); Task 2 adds retained-flag and pre-existing-file tests.\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/reviews/phase4.5-coverage-audit.md:13:- **MEDIUM:** retained flags (`--output`/`--cwd`/`--log`/`--grace`/`--heartbeat`) not exercised → added to Task 2.\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/reviews/phase4.5-coverage-audit.md:14:- **LOW:** row 4 mapping imprecise → split into row 4 (dead-code removal, Task 1) and row 4b (live heartbeat preserved, Task 5).\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/reviews/phase4.1-spec-dispatch-cli.md:8:- MEDIUM: retained-flag behavior under-covered → added a `--output` scenario asserting the `output`/`output_exists` result fields.\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/reviews/phase4.1-spec-dispatch-cli.md:9:- MEDIUM (security): the no-files rule didn't cover the removed control channel → added a scenario that a planted `control.json` cannot abort a dispatch.\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/specs/dispatch-cli/spec.md:17:The CLI SHALL accept `--model`, `--effort`, `--timeout`, `--sandbox`, `--config`, `--prompt-file`, `--prompt`, `--output`, `--cwd`, `--log`, `--json`, `--grace`, and `--heartbeat`.\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/specs/dispatch-cli/spec.md:23:#### Scenario: --output writes the worker's output artifact to the given path\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/specs/dispatch-cli/spec.md:24:- **WHEN** a dispatch is invoked with `--output p`\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/specs/dispatch-cli/spec.md:25:- **THEN** the worker's output artifact is written to `p`, and the JSON result's `output` field is `p` with `output_exists` true\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/specs/dispatch-cli/spec.md:28:A dispatch SHALL NOT create any files under `/tmp/darkfactory-dispatch/` or `~/.darkfactory/dispatches/`. User-specified `--log` and `--output` paths are written as directed and are out of scope for this prohibition.\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/specs/dispatch-cli/spec.md:31:- **WHEN** a dispatch completes with no user-specified `--log`/`--output` path under those locations\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/specs/dispatch-cli/spec.md:34:#### Scenario: A planted control file cannot abort a dispatch\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/specs/dispatch-cli/spec.md:35:- **WHEN** a `control.json` containing an abort request is present under the old `/tmp` dispatch path while a dispatch runs\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/specs/dispatch-cli/spec.md:36:- **THEN** the dispatch ignores it and runs to normal completion (the control-file abort channel no longer exists)\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/specs/dispatch-cli/spec.md:39:The CLI `--help` output SHALL NOT list the removed `--async` flag or the lifecycle subcommands named `status`, `wait`, and `result`. (Incidental prose about the JSON result object is acceptable.)\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/specs/synchronous-dispatch/spec.md:6:The dispatcher SHALL run a Codex worker to completion synchronously and emit exactly one structured JSON result object on stdout. In `--json` mode, stdout SHALL carry only that object; the worker's own output is consumed by the dispatcher (parsed as NDJSON events) and never forwarded to stdout, and all dispatcher events and diagnostics SHALL go to stderr. A `completed` result SHALL exit the dispatcher process 0; any `failed` or `timed_out` result SHALL exit it non-zero.\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/specs/synchronous-dispatch/spec.md:9:- **WHEN** a dispatch is run with `--json`, the worker exits 0, and (when `--output` was given) the output file exists\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/specs/synchronous-dispatch/spec.md:12:#### Scenario: Worker exits 0 but the requested output file is missing\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/specs/synchronous-dispatch/spec.md:13:- **WHEN** the worker exits 0 but `--output` was specified and the file was not created\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/specs/synchronous-dispatch/spec.md:24:### Requirement: Two-phase timeout\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/specs/synchronous-dispatch/spec.md:25:The dispatcher SHALL enforce `--timeout` by sending SIGTERM at the soft deadline, waiting a grace period, then sending SIGKILL, and SHALL report the outcome as a timed-out status.\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/specs/synchronous-dispatch/spec.md:27:#### Scenario: Worker exceeds the timeout\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/specs/synchronous-dispatch/spec.md:28:- **WHEN** a worker runs past its `--timeout`\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/specs/synchronous-dispatch/spec.md:29:- **THEN** the dispatcher sends SIGTERM, waits the grace period, sends SIGKILL if the worker is still alive, the JSON result has `status` equal to `\"timed_out\"`, and the dispatcher process exits non-zero\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/specs/synchronous-dispatch/spec.md:32:The dispatcher SHALL emit a heartbeat event to stderr at the heartbeat interval (default 15 seconds), carrying elapsed time and last activity, so a caller can distinguish a working worker from a dead one.\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/specs/synchronous-dispatch/spec.md:34:#### Scenario: Long-running dispatch emits heartbeats\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/specs/synchronous-dispatch/spec.md:35:- **WHEN** a dispatch runs longer than one heartbeat interval\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/specs/synchronous-dispatch/spec.md:36:- **THEN** stderr carries heartbeat events that include an `elapsed_s` value and a `last_activity` field, emitted at least once per interval\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/specs/synchronous-dispatch/spec.md:39:When the dispatcher terminates a worker, it SHALL also terminate the other processes in the worker's process group, leaving no orphaned processes from that group.\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/specs/synchronous-dispatch/spec.md:41:#### Scenario: Killing a worker kills its process group\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/specs/synchronous-dispatch/spec.md:42:- **WHEN** the dispatcher kills a timed-out worker that spawned child processes in its process group\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/specs/synchronous-dispatch/spec.md:46:The dispatcher SHALL terminate the worker if the dispatcher's own parent process exits, in all dispatches (this watch is always enabled).\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/specs/synchronous-dispatch/spec.md:52:### Requirement: Worker log capture\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/specs/synchronous-dispatch/spec.md:53:When `--log <path>` is given, the dispatcher SHALL write the worker's stdout and stderr to that path. Dispatcher events (heartbeats, diagnostics) are emitted on the dispatcher's own stderr.\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/specs/synchronous-dispatch/spec.md:55:#### Scenario: Caller tails a combined log\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/specs/synchronous-dispatch/spec.md:56:- **WHEN** a dispatch runs with `--log f` and the caller appends the dispatcher's stderr to the same file (`2>>f`)\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/specs/synchronous-dispatch/spec.md:57:- **THEN** `f` contains both the worker's output and the dispatcher's heartbeat events, and can be followed live with `tail -f`\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/reviews/phase5-contract.md:8:No CRITICAL/HIGH. 26 checks across 6 tasks. Testability: 17 [execution], 9 [output], 0 [inspection] (0% inspection — well under the 20%/task cap). Every dispatch-cli (1-7), synchronous-dispatch (1-9), and adversarial-sync-review (1-3) scenario is covered; traces verified by document order; exit codes match the code mapping.\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/reviews/phase5-contract.md:12:Round 2 (2 HIGH): \"no files after dispatch\" passes on old code (writes `status.json` mid-run, deletes on exit) → added an [output] source grep that the status/store/control internals are gone; missing-binary exit code was vague \"non-zero\" → pinned to exit 2 (`BinaryNotFound -> EXIT_CLI_ERROR`), exit 1 for other failures.\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/reviews/phase4.4-tasks.md:8:No CRITICAL/HIGH. Codex confirmed Task 2 is genuinely atomic for the `store_dir`/engine status/control removal and the dependency order is sound.\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/reviews/phase4.4-tasks.md:11:- MEDIUM (coverage): the spec's new regression tests (`--async`/lifecycle rejection, no `/tmp` or `~/.darkfactory/dispatches` files, planted `control.json` ignored, spawn-error JSON) were not explicitly mapped → added as integration-test outputs of Task 2.\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/reviews/phase2-ubiquitous-language.md:9:The glossary already covers this mission's domain (`Dispatcher`, `Dispatch`). The supervisor internals this change touches — two-phase timeout, heartbeat, process group, dispatch store, dispatch result — are mechanics that, per the `/language` inclusion bar, live in `tools/darkfactory-dispatch/README.md`, not the glossary. Removing the async subsystem introduces no new ambiguity-prone domain terms. Glossary left unchanged; no Codex artifact-review was dispatched because there is no changed artifact to review.\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/reviews/phase4.1-spec-synchronous-dispatch.md:9:- R1 HIGH: `--log f` + `2>f` truncation race → scenario now uses `2>>f` (append).\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/reviews/phase4.1-spec-synchronous-dispatch.md:10:- R2 HIGH: `completed` also requires the `--output` file present → success scenario amended + missing-output scenario added.\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/reviews/phase4.1-spec-synchronous-dispatch.md:11:- R3 HIGH: missing-output scenario didn't state the process exit → closed globally with the invariant \"any `failed`/`timed_out` result exits non-zero.\"\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/reviews/phase4.1-spec-synchronous-dispatch.md:12:- MEDIUM: process-group scoping (was \"any child processes\"); stdout purity (worker output consumed as NDJSON, not forwarded); spawn-error scenario added.\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/reviews/phase4.2-design.md:8:- (pass 1) status writes are at TWO `write_status_json_atomic` sites, not just the watchdog arm → design now names both.\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/reviews/phase4.2-design.md:9:- **HIGH (pass 2): compile-safe removal order.** `engine.rs` reads `spec.store_dir` for status-dir selection, cleanup, parent-death, and both status writes, so removing the field before its readers breaks the build → removal order now collapses the async-store + engine status/control removal into one compile-safe step (\"every task compiles at its commit\").\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/reviews/phase4.2-design.md:12:- LOW: `orphaned` is an async-lifecycle state, not a `DispatchStatus` variant → removed from the Type Catalog.\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/specs/adversarial-sync-review/spec.md:13:The `/adversarial` skill SHALL report a reviewer that completed successfully as complete, reading the dispatch result from the captured background output rather than from a dispatch id that does not survive the background shell.\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/mission/validations/task-5-scrutiny.md:13:- supervisor.rs test functions present + pass: `two_phase_timeout_escalates_from_sigterm_to_sigkill`, `kill_terminates_the_whole_process_group`, `parent_death_terminates_supervised_child`.\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/mission/validations/task-5-scrutiny.md:14:- engine.rs heartbeat test present + passes.\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/mission/validations/task-5-scrutiny.md:15:- combined-log test `log_file_combines_worker_output_and_redirected_dispatcher_events` present + passes.\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/mission/validations/task-5-scrutiny.md:18:0 P0/P1/P2; 2 advisory P3 (helper-name coupling in the parent-death test; SIGTERM-graceful path not exercised in this diff). Tests are non-tautological — combined-log asserts two independent event sources; timeout drives a real SIGTERM→SIGKILL against a TERM-ignoring child; parent-death verifies orphan termination via a real exiting parent.\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/mission/handoffs/task-3.md:11:- Verified `--json`, `--log`, `.status`, `BashOutput`, `REVIEW_COMPLETE`, and `REVIEW_FAILED` are present.\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/mission/validations/task-3-scrutiny.md:33:| Gate 5: Code review | PASS | Converted Step 2/Step 4 shell logic verified correct; see below. |\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/mission/validations/task-3-scrutiny.md:40:| Gate 12: Behavioral conformance | PASS | Status-branch logic executed in isolation across 5 cases; markers correct. |\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/mission/validations/task-3-scrutiny.md:51:| 3 | Skill reads dispatch `.status` from captured output; emits `REVIEW_COMPLETE` on `completed` and `REVIEW_FAILED` on `failed`/`timed_out` | PASS | execution | Lines 103-110 parse `.status`; isolated run of the branch produced `REVIEW_COMPLETE` only for `completed`+report-present, and `REVIEW_FAILED` for `failed`, `timed_out`, missing report, and dispatcher crash. |\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/mission/validations/task-3-scrutiny.md:69:and reported (with the log path) instead of claiming a completed report.\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/mission/validations/task-3-scrutiny.md:79:same flag set (`--model/--effort/--timeout/--sandbox/--prompt-file/--output/--cwd/\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/mission/validations/task-3-scrutiny.md:80:--log/--json 2>>\"$LOG_PATH\"`), same empty-output guard, same `.status` parse, same\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/mission/validations/task-3-scrutiny.md:84:output (`darkfactory-dispatch --help`: `\"status\":\"completed|timed_out|failed\"`).\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/mission/validations/task-3-scrutiny.md:92:- empty output (crash) -> `REVIEW_FAILED: dispatcher crashed with no output ...`\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/mission/briefs/task-3.md:12:- **Step 2 (Dispatch Codex reviewer):** remove `--async`; use `--json`; add `--log \"<log-path>\"` and redirect the dispatcher's stderr with `2>>\"<log-path>\"`. Capture the result and decide the outcome in the same backgrounded call, e.g.:\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/mission/briefs/task-3.md:15:    --model \"$DEFAULT_MODEL\" --effort high --timeout 900 \\\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/mission/briefs/task-3.md:17:    --prompt-file \"$PROMPT_PATH\" --output \"<codex-report-path>\" \\\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/mission/briefs/task-3.md:18:    --cwd \"$(pwd)\" --log \"<codex-log-path>\" --json 2>>\"<codex-log-path>\")\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/mission/briefs/task-3.md:21:    echo \"REVIEW_FAILED: dispatcher crashed with no output. Log: <codex-log-path>\"\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/mission/briefs/task-3.md:28:      echo \"REVIEW_FAILED: status $DISPATCH_STATUS${DISPATCH_ERROR:+; error: $DISPATCH_ERROR}. Log: <codex-log-path>\"\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/mission/briefs/task-3.md:33:- Remove the \"Do NOT pass `--json` alongside `--async`\" note and the `async_started`/`DISPATCH_ID` capture. Keep the note that `--output` writes Codex's final message, so the prompt still asks Codex to return the report as its final message and write no files.\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/mission/briefs/task-1.md:8:- `src/event.rs`: `CancellationToken`; `heartbeat_ticker`; the `StreamMode::Silent` and `StreamMode::Verbose` variants (production constructs only `StreamMode::Normal` — collapse `StreamMode` accordingly or remove unused variants); `Emitter::emit_heartbeat` (the no-interval one); and the event-local `DEFAULT_HEARTBEAT_INTERVAL_SECS` constant (distinct from the live one in `types.rs`).\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/mission/briefs/task-1.md:9:- Delete the tests that exist only to exercise the above: in `src/event.rs` the `stream_mode_filtering` and `heartbeat_ticker_can_be_cancelled` tests; in `tests/supervisor.rs` the `graceful_stop_*` tests and the singular `.arg(...)` usages; in `tests/engine.rs` any use of `StreamMode::Verbose` (switch it to `StreamMode::Normal`).\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/mission/briefs/task-1.md:11:### CRITICAL — do NOT touch the live heartbeat\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/mission/briefs/task-1.md:12:The live 15s heartbeat is `Emitter::emit_heartbeat_with_interval`, driven by the inline `heartbeat_interval` arm in `engine.rs`'s select loop. Leave it and `DEFAULT_HEARTBEAT_INTERVAL_SECS` in `types.rs` completely untouched. Only the *dead* helpers above are removed.\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/mission/briefs/task-1.md:18:- The named dead APIs are gone from `src/`; the live heartbeat path is unchanged.\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/mission/briefs/task-1.md:22:`darkfactory-dispatch` is a Rust process supervisor for Codex workers. It is being made synchronous-only by removing incidental machinery (async subsystem, control-file channel, status writes) and dead code. This task removes the pre-existing dead test-only code first, in isolation, so later tasks start clean.\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/mission/briefs/task-1.md:25:The crate lives at `tools/darkfactory-dispatch/` (there is NO root `Cargo.toml` — run all `cargo` commands from that directory). Modules: `main.rs` (entry), `cli.rs` (arg parsing), `engine.rs` (dispatch loop), `supervisor.rs` (process group, signals, parent-death), `event.rs` (event emitter), `types.rs` (data types). This task touches only `supervisor.rs`, `event.rs`, their tests, and the `#[expect(dead_code)]` annotations in `event.rs`/`main.rs`.\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/mission/briefs/task-1.md:37:Task 2 (remove the async subsystem and engine status/control) builds on the cleaned crate. No later task consumes a specific API from this task; the integration point is simply that the crate still builds and its retained tests pass.\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/mission/validations/task-6-scrutiny.md:31:| Gate 3: Tests | PASS | `79 passed, 0 failed, 1 ignored (98.8% pass rate)`. The 1 ignored is `parent_death_helper_spawns_supervised_child` (pre-existing `#[ignore]`, unrelated). Actual run rate 98.8% (over 90%), no WARNING. |\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/mission/validations/task-6-scrutiny.md:33:| Gate 5: Code review | PASS | Subagent review: clean. Removed `DispatchError` variants truly unconstructed; `StreamMode` removal changes no output/exit; `as_str()` returns identical strings; both call sites are mechanical swaps. |\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/mission/validations/task-6-scrutiny.md:40:| Gate 12: Behavioral conformance | PASS | Ran the real binary against the mock: both new tests pass by execution (`json_failed_dispatch_... ok`, `plain_dispatch_output_... ok`). |\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/mission/validations/task-6-scrutiny.md:42:| Gate 14: Diff coverage | PASS | Meaningful added production lines are covered: `as_str()` (types.rs 5/5 in tarpaulin; all three arms exercised across the suite), engine.rs:188 call site (engine.rs 348/364), cli.rs:147 plain-output call site exercised by the new `plain_dispatch_output` test. tarpaulin's 0/49 on cli.rs is an `assert_cmd` instrumentation artifact (separate binary), not a real gap. Effective diff coverage ~100%. |\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/mission/validations/task-6-scrutiny.md:43:| Gate 15: Test quality review | PASS | Subagent /test-quality: no findings. Both new tests parse output from the real compiled binary, assert on dispatcher-derived values (not inputs), and would fail under plausible regressions in