cal swaps. Smoke test and result JSON see the same strings.\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/mission/handoffs/task-2.md:7:- Engine watchdog control/status file machinery.\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/mission/handoffs/task-2.md:13:- Heartbeats, timeout/grace handling, process group isolation, parent-death detection.\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/mission/handoffs/task-2.md:22:- `--output`, `--cwd`, `--log`, `--grace`, `--heartbeat` still work.\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/mission/briefs/task-4.md:4:Update the documentation of `tools/darkfactory-dispatch/` to reflect the now synchronous-only dispatcher. The async subsystem, the lifecycle subcommands, the dispatch store, and the control-file/status machinery no longer exist (removed in Task 2); the docs must not describe them.\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/mission/briefs/task-4.md:7:- Remove the async-mode documentation: any \"Async dispatch\"/async-mode section, the `--async` flag from the flag table, the `status`/`wait`/`result` lifecycle subcommands, and the \"dispatch store\" (`~/.darkfactory/dispatches/<id>/`, `status.json`/`result.json`/`host.pid`/`events.jsonl`, 7-day pruning) section.\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/mission/briefs/task-4.md:8:- Remove or correct the async clause in the parent-death description (parent-death is now always on).\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/mission/briefs/task-4.md:9:- KEEP the \"Monitoring progress\" guidance and the `tail -f` example prominent — heartbeats still stream to the dispatcher's stderr; capturing them in a tailable file needs the caller to redirect stderr (`2>>log`), so keep that accurate.\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/mission/briefs/task-4.md:41:- Task 2 (eece9ea): synchronous-only dispatcher — removed `--async`, the `status`/`wait`/`result` subcommands, the dispatch store, the control-file/status machinery, `store_dir`, `LiveStatus`, and the `tracing` deps. Retained flags: `--model/--effort/--timeout/--sandbox/--config/--prompt-file/--prompt/--output/--cwd/--log/--json/--grace/--heartbeat`. Result JSON: `status` (`completed`/`failed`/`timed_out`), plus `exit_code`, `output`, `output_exists`, tokens, activity. Exit codes: 0 completed, 1 failed/timed_out, 2 CLI error.\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/mission/validations/task-1-scrutiny.md:9:- **Error handling smells:** 0 matches in 3 changed production lines (0 per KLOC). The 3 added `src/` lines all live inside the `#[cfg(test)]` module of `event.rs`; the only `.expect(...)` uses carry a non-empty message (\"emit heartbeat\"), a safe pattern. Locations: none.\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/mission/validations/task-1-scrutiny.md:19:| Gate 5: Code review | PASS | No bugs, security, or logic issues. See findings below. |\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/mission/validations/task-1-scrutiny.md:24:| Gate 10: Security review | N/A | Diff touches no auth, secrets, user input, network, or filesystem trust boundaries. It deletes a SIGTERM/SIGKILL helper but the surviving signal paths (`kill_soft`, `kill`) are unchanged. |\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/mission/validations/task-1-scrutiny.md:34:| 1 | `grep -rnE \"fn graceful_stop\\|fn heartbeat_ticker\\|struct CancellationToken\\|fn emit_heartbeat\\b\\|StreamMode::(Silent\\|Verbose)\\|StdinMode::Piped\\|fn pid\\b\" src/` returns no matches | PASS | execution | grep over `tools/darkfactory-dispatch/src/` returned no lines (exit 1). All 7 named dead APIs are gone. |\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/mission/validations/task-1-scrutiny.md:38:## Critical preservation check (live heartbeat path)\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/mission/validations/task-1-scrutiny.md:39:**PASS.** The live production heartbeat was NOT removed:\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/mission/validations/task-1-scrutiny.md:40:- `emit_heartbeat_with_interval` still defined at `src/event.rs:166` and called from `src/engine.rs:205`.\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/mission/validations/tas