artbeat, process group, parent-death) is preserved.\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/mission/briefs/task-2.md:37:`darkfactory-dispatch` supervises Codex workers. It is being made synchronous-only. This is the core removal task: the async lifecycle (a `--async` flag, `status`/`wait`/`result` subcommands, and a `~/.darkfactory/dispatches/<ulid>/` store) and the engine's control-file + status-file machinery are removed, leaving the single synchronous path production already uses.\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/mission/briefs/task-2.md:40:Crate at `tools/darkfactory-dispatch/` (NO root `Cargo.toml`; run all `cargo` commands there). Modules: `main.rs` (entry), `cli.rs` (clap + `DispatchSpec`), `engine.rs` (`dispatch()` loop), `supervisor.rs` (process group, signals, parent-death), `event.rs` (emitter), `types.rs` (`DispatchSpec`, `DispatchResult`, `DispatchStatus`, `DispatchError`, ...). Follow the crate's `CLAUDE.md` rules (Gallant boundary: engine owns dispatch logic, CLI only parses/formats; `thiserror` not `anyhow`; `pub(crate)`; `#[expect]` not `#[allow]`; no `#[serde(flatten/untagged)]`; stdout=result JSON, stderr=diagnostics).\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/mission/briefs/task-2.md:47:- `DispatchResult` — the structured result (status, exit code, output, output_exists, ...); `types.rs`.\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/mission/briefs/task-2.md:53:- Removed dead test-only APIs from `supervisor.rs` and `event.rs` (`graceful_stop`, `RunHandle::pid` + `RunState.pid`, `StdinMode::Piped`, singular `arg`, `CancellationToken`, `heartbeat_ticker`, `Emitter::emit_heartbeat`, event-local heartbeat const, `StreamMode::Silent`/`Verbose`) and their tests; resolved `#[expect(dead_code)]` in `event.rs` + `main.rs`.\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/mission/briefs/task-2.md:54:- The live heartbeat path (`emit_heartbeat_with_interval` + the inline `heartbeat_interval` arm in `engine.rs`) is intact. `types.rs` `#[expect(dead_code)]` + `DispatchError` variants 