ort channel (`control.json` watchdog), the automatic `/tmp` `status.json` writes, dead test-only code, `LiveStatus`, `DispatchSpec.store_dir`, single-variant `StreamMode`, unused `DispatchError` variants, and the `tracing`/`tracing-subscriber` deps. It moved the spawn-error `failed` JSON into the unified synchronous path. It converted the `/adversarial` skill from `--async` + `wait` to synchronous `--json` + `run_in_background` + `BashOutput`. It must PRESERVE all supervision: process-group isolation (`setpgid`), two-phase SIGTERM→SIGKILL timeout, 15s heartbeats (`emit_heartbeat_with_interval` on stderr), parent-death (now always-on), and the structured JSON result.\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/mission/reviews/phase9-adversarial-prompt.md:11:- **Supervision regressions:** did removing the watchdog arm, control-file, or status writes accidentally break the timeout state machine, heartbeat emission, process-group teardown, or parent-death? Is parent-death genuinely always-on now?\nopenspec/changes/dispatch-sync-only/mission/reviews/phase9-adversarial-prompt.md:15:- **Behavior-change risks:** does the result JSON schema, the `--log` capture, or the retained flags (`--grace`/`--heartbeat`/`--output`/`--cwd`) behave the same as before?\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
