{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_33","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba tools/darkfactory-dispatch/README.md | sed -n '70,200p'\"","aggregated_output":"error: Can't create the symlink for multishells at \"/run/user/1001/fnm_multishells/8_1782868060398\". Maybe there are some issues with permissions for the directory? Read-only file system (os error 30)\n    70\t```\n    71\t\n    72\t## Usage\n    73\t\n    74\t### Dispatch\n    75\t\n    76\tDispatch a task and wait for the result:\n    77\t\n    78\t```bash\n    79\tdarkfactory-dispatch \\\n    80\t  --model gpt-5.5 \\\n    81\t  --effort high \\\n    82\t  --timeout 1800 \\\n    83\t  --sandbox workspace-write \\\n    84\t  --config 'sandbox_workspace_write.writable_roots=[\".git\"]' \\\n    85\t  --prompt-file brief.md \\\n    86\t  --output handoff.md \\\n    87\t  --cwd /path/to/repo \\\n    88\t  --log dispatch.log \\\n    89\t  --json 2>>dispatch.log\n    90\t```\n    91\t\n    92\tThe dispatch result is a single JSON object on stdout. In `--json` mode stdout carries **only** that one object; all events, heartbeats, and diagnostics go to stderr. Do not merge the two streams (`2>&1`) when parsing the result -- the concatenated event lines will make `jq` or `serde_json` fail. Redirect stderr elsewhere (e.g. `2>>dispatch.log`), as the examples above do.\n    93\t\n    94\t```json\n    95\t{\n    96\t  \"status\": \"completed\",\n    97\t  \"dispatch_id\": \"01KQ3XPQZM6R34H360BF6B8W82\",\n    98\t  \"duration_ms\": 53311,\n    99\t  \"exit_code\": 0,\n   100\t  \"signal\": null,\n   101\t  \"output\": \"handoff.md\",\n   102\t  \"output_exists\": true,\n   103\t  \"error\": null,\n   104\t  \"tokens\": {\n   105\t    \"input\": 136538,\n   106\t    \"output\": 1407,\n   107\t    \"reasoning\": 0\n   108\t  },\n   109\t  \"activity\": {\n   110\t    \"files_changed\": [\"src/lib.rs\", \"src/main.rs\"],\n   111\t    \"files_read\": [\"Cargo.toml\", \"README.md\"],\n   112\t    \"commands_run\": [\"cargo test\", \"cargo clippy\"],\n   113\t    \"tool_calls\": 5,\n   114\t    \"parse_errors\": 0\n   115\t  }\n   116\t}\n   117\t```\n   118\t\n   119\t### Monitoring progress\n   120\t\n   121\tThe dispatcher emits NDJSON events to stderr during a dispatch:\n   122\t\n   123\t```jsonl\n   124\t{\"type\":\"dispatch_start\",\"dispatch_id\":\"...\",\"ts\":\"...\",\"engine\":\"codex\",\"model\":\"gpt-5.5\"}\n   125\t{\"type\":\"heartbeat\",\"dispatch_id\":\"...\",\"ts\":\"...\",\"elapsed_s\":15,\"last_activity\":\"running: cargo test\"}\n   126\t{\"type\":\"command_run\",\"dispatch_id\":\"...\",\"ts\":\"...\",\"command\":\"cargo test\"}\n   127\t{\"type\":\"file_write\",\"dispatch_id\":\"...\",\"ts\":\"...\",\"file\":\"src/lib.rs\"}\n   128\t{\"type\":\"heartbeat\",\"dispatch_id\":\"...\",\"ts\":\"...\",\"elapsed_s\":30,\"last_activity\":\"writing: src/lib.rs\"}\n   129\t{\"type\":\"timeout_warning\",\"dispatch_id\":\"...\",\"ts\":\"...\",\"elapsed_s\":1800}\n   130\t{\"type\":\"dispatch_end\",\"dispatch_id\":\"...\",\"ts\":\"...\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"duration_ms\":53311}\n   131\t```\n   132\t\n   133\tTo watch progress live, redirect stderr to the log file and tail it:\n   134\t\n   135\t```bash\n   136\tdarkfactory-dispatch ... --json 2>>dispatch.log &\n   137\ttail -f dispatch.log\n   138\t```\n   139\t\n   140\t## Flags\n   141\t\n   142\t| Flag | Default | Description |\n   143\t|------|---------|-------------|\n   144\t| `--model` | `gpt-5.5` | Codex model to use |\n   145\t| `--effort` | (none) | Reasoning effort (maps to `-c model_reasoning_effort`) |\n   146\t| `--timeout` | `900` | Seconds before soft timeout fires (SIGTERM) |\n   147\t| `--grace` | half of timeout, min 1s | Seconds between soft timeout and hard timeout (SIGKILL) |\n   148\t| `--heartbeat` | `15` | Seconds between heartbeat events emitted to stderr |\n   149\t| `--sandbox` | `workspace-write` | Codex sandbox mode |\n   150\t| `--config` | (none) | Repeatable. Key=value passed to Codex `-c` flag |\n   151\t| `--prompt` | (none) | Task prompt (mutually exclusive with `--prompt-file`; must be non-empty) |\n   152\t| `--prompt-file` | (none) | Read prompt from file (for large briefs; an empty or whitespace-only file is a CLI error) |\n   153\t| `--output` | (none) | Path for Codex to write results (passed to `-o`) |\n   154\t| `--cwd` | current dir | Working directory for the Codex process |\n   155\t| `--log` | (none) | File to capture Codex stdout and stderr |\n   156\t| `--json` | false | Emit dispatch result as JSON on stdout |\n   157\t\n   158\t## Two-phase timeout\n   159\t\n   160\tThe dispatcher enforces a configurable two-phase timeout:\n   161\t\n   162\t1. **Soft timeout** (at `--timeout` seconds): Sends SIGTERM to the process group and emits a `timeout_warning` event. The worker has a chance to flush partial results.\n   163\t2. **Hard timeout** (at `--timeout` + `--grace` seconds): Sends SIGKILL to the process group. The worker is forcibly terminated.\n   164\t\n   165\tThe grace period defaults to half the timeout with a minimum of 1 second.\n   166\t\n   167\tIf the worker exits cleanly after SIGTERM (during the grace period), the dispatch result reports `timed_out` with the worker's final output preserved.\n   168\t\n   169\t## Process group isolation\n   170\t\n   171\tEvery Codex worker runs in its own process group (via `setpgid`). When the dispatcher sends SIGTERM or SIGKILL, the signal goes to the entire group -- not just the Codex process, but every shell command and subprocess it spawned. This prevents orphaned processes from accumulating.\n   172\t\n   173\t## Parent-death detection\n   174\t\n   175\tThe dispatcher detects when its parent process (the orchestrator) dies and kills the worker to prevent orphans:\n   176\t\n   177\t- **macOS**: Uses kqueue with `EVFILT_PROC` + `NOTE_EXIT` to watch the parent PID\n   178\t- **Linux**: Uses `PR_SET_PDEATHSIG` to arrange SIGKILL on parent death\n   179\t\n   180\t## Exit codes\n   181\t\n   182\t| Code | Meaning |\n   183\t|------|---------|\n   184\t| 0 | Dispatch completed successfully |\n   185\t| 1 | Dispatch failed or timed out |\n   186\t| 2 | CLI error (bad arguments, missing or empty prompt, file read error) |\n   187\t\n   188\t## Dispatch result status\n   189\t\n   190\t| Status | Meaning |\n   191\t|--------|---------|\n   192\t| `completed` | Worker exited 0 and output file exists (if `--output` was specified) |\n   193\t| `timed_out` | Two-phase timeout fired. `error.retryable` is true. |\n   194\t| `failed` | Worker exited non-zero, output file missing, or spawn error |\n   195\t\n   196\t## Development\n   197\t\n   198\t```bash\n   199\tmake build     # Debug build\n   200\tmake test      # Run 78 Rust tests\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
